{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01111",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.78,
      "end_seconds": 3.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Good morning. I've just opened your notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.67,
      "end_seconds": 7.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Hello, thanks for fitting me in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 9.61,
      "end_seconds": 18.12,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.81,
      "end_seconds": 26.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.81,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here. How are things, what's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.22,
      "end_seconds": 34.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "Hmm, it's a pounding heart. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.73,
      "end_seconds": 42.74,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.42,
      "end_seconds": 62.54,
      "duration_seconds": 18.12,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, about... well, about two weeks. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. My neighbour said I should get it looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.89,
      "end_seconds": 66.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.21,
      "end_seconds": 71.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "A five out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.3,
      "end_seconds": 75.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.75,
      "end_seconds": 92.02,
      "duration_seconds": 15.27,
      "text": "Oh, when it starts I tend to get sudden hunger as well. So, you know, I've also been feeling confused at times, for three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.69,
      "end_seconds": 97.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.88,
      "end_seconds": 100.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.1,
      "end_seconds": 102.89,
      "duration_seconds": 0.79,
      "text": "Mm-hmm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.19,
      "end_seconds": 112.68,
      "duration_seconds": 8.49,
      "text": "Hmm, I have kidney disease, for five years. I, I have high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.04,
      "end_seconds": 126.16,
      "duration_seconds": 12.12,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Right, so diabetes is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.97,
      "end_seconds": 131.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "No, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.03,
      "end_seconds": 136.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.8,
      "end_seconds": 141.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.99,
      "end_seconds": 145.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.54,
      "end_seconds": 150.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.72,
      "end_seconds": 154.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.55,
      "end_seconds": 161.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.53,
      "end_seconds": 168.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 168.88,
      "end_seconds": 175.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.67,
      "text": "So, it's glibenclamide, 5 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.67,
      "end_seconds": 179.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 181.19,
      "end_seconds": 187.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.5,
      "text": "About about three months. She takes valsartan, 80 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.1,
      "end_seconds": 202.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any blurred vision, fainting or seizure?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.12,
      "end_seconds": 206.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.59,
      "end_seconds": 209.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Any slurred speech or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.32,
      "end_seconds": 217.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.83,
      "end_seconds": 221.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.23,
      "end_seconds": 225.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.64,
      "end_seconds": 232.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.49,
      "end_seconds": 237.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Actually, that's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.99,
      "end_seconds": 242.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.34,
      "end_seconds": 257.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.49,
      "end_seconds": 283.37,
      "duration_seconds": 10.88,
      "text": "Okay: weight 93 kilos, height 156 centimetres, heart rate 78. And saturation 98 percent, temperature is 36.5 degrees, BP is 114 over 73."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.88,
      "end_seconds": 285.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.49,
      "end_seconds": 289.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.1,
      "end_seconds": 296.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Alright, I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.32,
      "end_seconds": 300.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.28,
      "end_seconds": 319.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "Your fingerprick sugar now is normal and your heart rate is steady."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.32,
      "end_seconds": 326.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.97,
      "end_seconds": 351.7,
      "duration_seconds": 11.73,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, it points towards episodes of low blood sugar related to diabetes treatment. I'm sending you for blood tests because of low sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.32,
      "end_seconds": 355.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.35,
      "end_seconds": 372.21,
      "duration_seconds": 15.86,
      "text": "Never skip meals when you take the sugar tablet, and keep glucose tablets or juice with you. Book a review after the blood tests. Let me check I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 376.27,
      "end_seconds": 382.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "So, I come back after the blood tests. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.91,
      "end_seconds": 387.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.74,
      "end_seconds": 392.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}